OOZEMeter is hand-written static HTML. It has never used Jekyll, and Jekyll
processing was pure liability: on 2026-08-14 a research document containing the
site's own canonical-truth tokens ({{s:2026-07}}) was committed, Liquid tried to
parse them as template syntax, and pages-build-deployment failed on every push
for two days while daily-collection stayed green.

The failure was invisible because the wrong workflow was being watched. The
robot collected, the gates passed, the commits landed, and the site did not
deploy.

This file disables Jekyll entirely. Any file in this repository may now contain
{{ }} without breaking the deploy, which matters because {{ }} is the token
syntax the whole narrative gate is built on.
